nally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](images/3c/3cfdf7d548c430f225a78fa6c4d915d69207f0a1c090d13cdd530c90865731ef.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387056 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129219 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "490982ac-6197-58eb-8d94-2ef28d659d50" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadrants Where a Function Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec5171c3-9b89-5b66-be82-6a7a96386a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e0/e019652dcfef9bb06dcecb42c1544e93b2f2909cfc1a40aac1eee3cf24f73e7e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387058} {:answer/id #uuid "9805a50f-0f5d-5181-bc78-cc625a280c94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6c/6cd862eaf47308e250abc6cd4016bcb84132de849b289753751840f9c44c107f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387059} {:answer/id #uuid "3936bc39-c5d9-5224-a86e-f6002674711a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4e/4ea9e14e3150f7566cae93bd241c8c9c1541f0f5c447066760ae26176491fe6a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387060} {:answer/id #uuid "37343435-1ffb-5cf3-987f-0dbd92e7dd64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/59/596e25c1d1f8a0e738d8853c17c77c2f6174a2c314a94ce1674f37b3a4c5c72b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387061} {:answer/id #uuid "09a69779-86ba-5e16-bc74-deb794663e13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/03/03b7fe2ba61cbe2608c37a78c82001f6a1fdebdb59f0be0785d55ee119ba8ff4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3936bc39-c5d9-5224-a86e-f6002674711a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4e/4ea9e14e3150f7566cae93bd241c8c9c1541f0f5c447066760ae26176491fe6a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387060} :answer-field/id #uuid "8657a476-279d-5261-9e1b-ae66167785a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "075fb7b7-04bf-5658-846e-155b9f5d2466" :question/math-academy-id "q-121261" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y)={x}^{2}{y}^{3}.$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)\\le 0?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](images/c4/c44c38febc908fe5e941978bf44bab2e2cb4bd250765950d84f9294c9c4c9c4b.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](images/20/209576cd78e9beb1c0f7a9bce8267163df1668a830ffc5c06918f8a726600fbe.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | ${x}^{2}$ | ${y}^{3}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\le 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](images/02/02043b6cfae2cf7987b7df192143b82af474e75b7cfbfa4141a318c9aaed51e5.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256527 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129219 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "490982ac-6197-58eb-8d94-2ef28d659d50" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Quadrants Where a Function Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f4ca1fb-1e0b-53d6-b205-b13a5f751aba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/37/37000a15f2b6164932675c0f0e6dd78fa0ef3015dcc25b27d7dce139e8a1ce4b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253943} {:answer/id #uuid "59d5fb97-bde7-5ee9-923a-9c291568559a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8fde51124507af53cd4b653856f12976a675dc4bf10a274c84623797ad8e1f2c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254455} {:answer/id #uuid "64b384c1-0cea-5efb-8c4b-1bc3a0ea3c30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4e/4ea9e14e3150f7566cae93bd241c8c9c1541f0f5c447066760ae26176491fe6a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254573} {:answer/id #uuid "960053fc-39f1-5a4a-9da8-d5e665897e66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/59/596e25c1d1f8a0e738d8853c17c77c2f6174a2c314a94ce1674f37b3a4c5c72b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254993} {:answer/id #uuid "b6234e2d-0098-5b5f-bb2d-8373b46409f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/03/03b7fe2ba61cbe2608c37a78c82001f6a1fdebdb59f0be0785d55ee119ba8ff4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59d5fb97-bde7-5ee9-923a-9c291568559a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8fde51124507af53cd4b653856f12976a675dc4bf10a274c84623797ad8e1f2c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254455} :answer-field/id #uuid "42a29a0c-b99a-593a-a9a2-866370b09c15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256047}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4512ace0-4828-5c4a-8b31-1ca187b0fe9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-121262" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y)=-{x}^{2}{y}^{2}.$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)\\le 0?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](images/c4/c44c38febc908fe5e941978bf44bab2e2cb4bd250765950d84f9294c9c4c9c4b.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](images/20/209576cd78e9beb1c0f7a9bce8267163df1668a830ffc5c06918f8a726600fbe.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-{x}^{2}$ | ${y}^{2}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(-1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\le 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](images/fc/fc2a67dd63a482a37cf91c66c1b9fde01ea8c26ba0e3d6f7b8a62c112aae4bb0.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256528 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092167 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c7ab50-5a8b-5bcd-8483-cec8bf6bd3ce" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Trigonometric Equation Involving Tangent with Non-Special Angles"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "624591d9-0ec0-5462-b1e2-3d6aa9b885a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={86}^{∘},{266}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254552} {:answer/id #uuid "7062eef4-788f-51e3-aa7b-52b2d54bafbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={71}^{∘},{251}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254664} {:answer/id #uuid "7dde2698-fca4-5a9b-a33f-43540cf60d9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={74}^{∘},{254}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254786} {:answer/id #uuid "9369f0d8-3198-503d-b105-ae3c5411f90c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={80}^{∘},{260}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254963} {:answer/id #uuid "b7a71150-8b44-54e5-91f5-149720230ccd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={93}^{∘},{273}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "624591d9-0ec0-5462-b1e2-3d6aa9b885a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={86}^{∘},{266}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254552} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d9c5bc8-91f2-50d7-9c46-59537ac06b41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18b86489-8289-5d54-8044-fd38997410d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-121264" :question/problem "Solve the equation $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=15$ for ${0}^{∘}\\le x<{360}^{∘},$ rounded to the nearest integer." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(15)=86.185\\,925{…}^{∘}≈{86.19}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${86.19}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={86.19}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}={180}^{∘}+{86.19}^{∘}={266.19}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are\n\n$$\nx={86}^{∘},{266}^{∘}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179702 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ef881ff-71d4-5268-9cac-32c478dc02a5" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regions in the Plane Where a Function Is Positive or Negative"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "742f1bc2-d4ad-5ba5-aefd-e9a9aee172d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/95/9505947a6ab1ebfca0aedaeec8cde50e8859dfa7bc2b349833c9d26bd849748b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387072} {:answer/id #uuid "a74d4b2d-58cb-5696-b2f5-694615021391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8e/8eac178458e8d2b832f7b96fa5d54fedf94be2a9574666aae48c88fe254a8629.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387073} {:answer/id #uuid "8a268c86-1f9d-59cb-9640-aafa1890e479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/87/870d9de880f857a1fe66851ae115575955efb12b4cd651279d7494b4cb99d022.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387074} {:answer/id #uuid "21ee3236-f1d0-512e-85a7-9eee61acbbf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/85/85074c62b73199b0dd1ad8427339c58dae3e1d4ae1df014d94415aea57f24410.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387075} {:answer/id #uuid "733a2a66-7f59-58dd-a838-3cb393b88951" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ea/ea79645ad6bf13be7399d8a46d18c7b99e1f2c40d3a6c500ee3710e79fdfddb3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21ee3236-f1d0-512e-85a7-9eee61acbbf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/85/85074c62b73199b0dd1ad8427339c58dae3e1d4ae1df014d94415aea57f24410.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387075} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c8ebeba-ce4d-5520-ac7b-bafdeabb3251" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6bb23e0c-4a26-596c-aca7-3529c2ce3d72" :question/math-academy-id "q-121275" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x,y)=(x+2)(2-y).$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)<0?$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=-2$ and $y=2.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have a strict inequality, we use dashed lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](images/38/38f5235039b0a5800651759e8da98166451ab72d25e7eaa9772c10b68c3618ff.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](images/a6/a68d4ca3939349cef83c3c84117df44ddacf49d587b1bc8a871918f62d9b6516.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(x+2)$ | $(2-y)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(-3,3)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(-1,3)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-3,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)<0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](images/10/1055b7667e7b1c6d27ad7a9d28ec74ae7ed58dac262ae83b5c4028dcee3f9312.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8033e21-86ab-5dc6-8060-a0b5c134bf9d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regions Where a Function Is Positive or Negative Using a Sign Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa97b40a-e3d1-56c2-a3d3-fd9806c8b0d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400039} {:answer/id #uuid "6f760736-7136-5c51-8cad-d132bbb01cf6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $-$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $+$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400040} {:answer/id #uuid "a46a9208-8eef-5439-8528-e589bb68eb22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400041} {:answer/id #uuid "d28274c5-4356-52b1-85ec-470cdcdf78d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $-$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400042} {:answer/id #uuid "2b226ba3-7173-5ec9-acca-6026e662e178" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a46a9208-8eef-5439-8528-e589bb68eb22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400041} :answer-field/id #uuid "57afd616-b198-5c2a-93b3-d4e43c9661c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9195bf5b-e185-53ad-970f-942b816b9aec" :question/math-academy-id "q-121278" :question/problem "Consider the expression $f(x,y)=(x+1)(2-y).$ What are the missing entries in the sign table of $f(x,y),$ shown below?\n\n| $y>2$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<2$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<-1$ | $x>-1$ |" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=-1$ and $y=2.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/d5/d5d7c89d619aa13d7fea8bc1260a08cb8678fb260e4431508c5f4c8c53e7ba5e.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](images/6c/6cce64627f21f6cc17efc789614a0bd582ded827a0938f01c9b756e0cb461862.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(x+1)$ | $(2-y)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(-2,3)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(0,3)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-2,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(0,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](images/c2/c24cc3ab0812bfae6834ff8c3a68668c3925f6e39e29a453ea6bc27fbc9f6c74.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the table as follows:\n\n| $y>2$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<2$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<-1$ | $x>-1$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400051 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179701 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8033e21-86ab-5dc6-8060-a0b5c134bf9d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regions Where a Function Is Positive or Negative Using a Sign Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89a56145-d991-5f19-9125-7dfeb8c19018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $-$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $+$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400053} {:answer/id #uuid "06d8b15d-ffbd-5909-a889-264a17e6ec09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400054} {:answer/id #uuid "ff298d2d-031a-50d5-a2e0-d484276129ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400055} {:answer/id #uuid "bc19913c-5667-515a-bb6f-f55140f312eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $-$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400056} {:answer/id #uuid "af5764ad-7d4d-52f1-b5b0-d4fb0b6a16fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af5764ad-7d4d-52f1-b5b0-d4fb0b6a16fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400057} :answer-field/id #uuid "72a057d8-e342-52dd-a1fb-abc1e06dc5c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400052}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76c193df-21ad-5c48-bc98-a6dcd7963d51" :question/math-academy-id "q-121322" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x,y)=-x(y-1)^{2}.$ What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x,y)?$\n\n| $y>1$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<1$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=1.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/ef/ef935d673ddc4fa3b66305717f495914c194be2abff63611f8f6be6763e469ce.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](images/6f/6f2f29dbb53e8c20d963cc48c89af73b1c806985bc77842cbe28b882305ede32.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-x$ | $(y-1)^{2}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,2)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,2)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,0)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,0)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](images/71/71aceb11f3056308300e3e5c9587d76a281379964caab83f640a6924ffd94298.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>1$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<1$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 